@simon-mo thanks for the review. Updates since your approval:

- `/checkpoint/resume` is now `/checkpoint/restore`, and the `resuming` state is now `restoring`, matching the existing `checkpoint_restore` underneath in AsyncLLM.
- The `/checkpoint/*` routes are attached only with `--enable-sleep-mode`, as the fault-tolerance and profiler routes are only attached with their flags. Without sleep mode they could only refuse. The routes now also document their status codes.

